{"name":"Bouquet","hex":"#a78199","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bouquet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bouquet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower bouquet","blocks":[{"text":"A flower bouquet is a collection of flowers in a creative arrangement. Flower bouquets can be arranged for the decor of homes or public buildings or may be handheld. Several popular shapes and styles classify handheld bouquets, including nosegay, crescent, and cascading bouquets. Flower bouquets are often given for special occasions such as birthdays, anniversaries or funerals. They are also used extensively in weddings and at the Olympic medal ceremonies. Bouquets arranged in vases or planters for home decor can be placed in traditional or modern styles. According to the culture, symbolism may be attached to the types of flowers used."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_bouquet"},{"title":"Gift basket","blocks":[{"text":"A gift basket or fruit basket is typically a gift delivered to the recipient at their home or workplace. A variety of gift baskets exist: some contain fruit; while others might contain dry or canned foods such as tea, crackers and jam; or the basket might include a combination of fruit and dried good items. Gourmet gift baskets typically include exotic fruit, and often include quality cheese and wine, as well as other nonfood items. Gift baskets are often sent for special occasions—such as holidays—or as a thank-you or congratulations gift. In certain occasions, it is given as a sympathy gift or a condolence gift during funerals. In some countries in Asia, people use fruit baskets as decoration. They either eat it after the funeral service where the casket is laid in the cemetery or they leave the fruit baskets at their graves to let the dead rest in peace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Wrapped_fruit_basket.jpg/330px-Wrapped_fruit_basket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gift_basket"},{"title":"Bouquet (Gwen Stefani album)","blocks":[{"text":"Bouquet is the fifth studio album by American singer-songwriter Gwen Stefani. It was released on November 15, 2024, by Interscope Records, and was her first album in almost seven years, the last being 2017's You Make It Feel Like Christmas. Work started on the record in February 2020, when Stefani wrote a song called \"Cry Happy\", that inspired her to make a new album. Departing from the dance-pop of her previous albums, Bouquet is more reminiscent of 1970s pop rock and the country music her husband, Blake Shelton, is known for."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Gwen_Stefani_%E2%80%93_Bouquet_%28album_cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bouquet_(Gwen_Stefani_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg/500px-Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg/500px-Onam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh flowers are arranged in front of houses to celebrate Onam, a major celebration in \nKerala, India.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOnam_Flower_Arrangement.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/500px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/1280px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg/500px-Ikebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Japanese ikebana flower bouquet in a vase","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIkebana_-_Yoshiko_Nakamura_01B.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg/500px-Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg/1280px-Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg/500px-Beach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Beach wedding bouquet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_Wedding_Bouquet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg/120px-Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg/250px-Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg/120px-Kytice_a_formul%C3%A1%C5%99_p%C5%99i_uzav%C5%99en%C3%AD_registrovan%C3%A9ho_pratnerstv%C3%AD.jpg?u